---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// Copyright (c) 2024-2026 We-Amp B.V.
//
// Home further reading: four docs and blog cards, just above the closing
// panel.
//
// The markup keeps the indentation it has inside the page layout: the build
// does not compress HTML, so this indentation is the whitespace of the page.
// The class names are styled by the page's global style block in
// src/pages/index.astro.
---

  <section class="home-reading" aria-labelledby="s-reading">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <h2 id="s-reading" class="eyebrow">Further reading</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
          <a
            href="/docs/configuration/"
            class="card-resource"
            data-umami-event="cta_home_featured_docs_configuration"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow text-text-body">Docs</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-text-body">Configuration</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-body text-text-muted">
              Configuration options for Apache and nginx: directives, cache modes, worker settings,
              and per-location overrides.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-interactive inline-flex items-center gap-1">
              Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </p>
          </a>
          <a
            href="/docs/filters/"
            class="card-resource"
            data-umami-event="cta_home_featured_docs_filters"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow text-text-body">Docs</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-text-body">PageSpeed filters reference</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-body text-text-muted">
              Every rewrite filter and what it does: image transcoding, CSS and JS minification,
              combining, spriting, IPRO, and domain mapping.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-interactive inline-flex items-center gap-1">
              Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </p>
          </a>
          <a
            href="/blog/economics-of-image-optimization/"
            class="card-resource"
            data-umami-event="cta_home_blog_economics_images"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow text-text-body">Blog</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-text-body">
              Image optimization cost: self-hosted vs CDN (2026)
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-body text-text-muted">
              Cost comparison at 100K, 1M, and 10M monthly image requests &mdash; with break-even
              analysis against self-hosted optimization.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-interactive inline-flex items-center gap-1">
              Read post <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </p>
          </a>
          <a
            href="/blog/mod-pagespeed-alternatives/"
            class="card-resource"
            data-umami-event="cta_home_blog_mps_alternatives"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow text-text-body">Blog</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-text-body">
              mod_pagespeed Alternatives in 2026
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-body text-text-muted">
              The original mod_pagespeed and ngx_pagespeed &mdash; developed at Google &mdash; are
              no longer actively developed. Here is where to go instead.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-interactive inline-flex items-center gap-1">
              Read post <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
